// The game's SDR display mapping (its last pass: the world's picture to the screen, Render.DisplayMappingVersion 5,
// SdrPeakLuma 200, as the game comes), measured on the game on 2026-11-21 and made into two tables for world shaders
// (world_shader.h: t8, t9, reskate_shown and reskate_unshown). Every mix of 27 levels a channel, 1/64 to 128 in half
// stops, was drawn into the picture before that pass and read back off an SDR screen at render scale 100%. The mapping
// is not one curve a channel: a bright, saturated colour's other channels are lifted toward white, and in the middle
// they are pushed down. The inverse was solved from the forward table, read as the shaders read it, by least squares in
// sRGB: a colour past what the mapping can show is the nearest one it can. Not edited by hand.
